\begin{tabular}{llccc}\toprule
Scenario & Learner & Accuracy & Nucleonic vs DM & Strange recall\\\midrule\input{tables/tab_boot}\\\bottomrule\end{tabular}\end{table}
\paragraph{Population size.} Figure~\ref{fig:lc} shows the accuracy as a function of the number of training EoS (54 to 216). Without noise the logistic regression is already at @@lc_ALL_0_LogReg_25@@\% with 54 training EoS and the MLP ensemble at @@lc_ALL_0_MLP-ens_50@@\% with 108, against @@lc_ALL_0_MLP-ens_100@@\% with 216; under NICER-like errors plus a 20\% $f$-mode the accuracy is @@lc_NICERpf20_LogReg_25@@--@@lc_NICERpf20_MLP-ens_100@@\% at every size. The plateau therefore does not appear to result from too few EoS, and a larger population of the same kind is unlikely to change the numbers.
